WEBVTT

NOTE Visual description and on-screen text; the film has music and no spoken narration.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
A field of dots fills a dark blue screen as a counter climbs to 5,288,766. On-screen text: New Yorkers live in designated primary-care shortage areas. HRSA, as of September 30, 2026.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:13.000
The dots fly together into the shape of New York State, and its 62 counties fill in shades of blue. On-screen text: 1.8 million adults in New York are estimated to live with diagnosed diabetes. From 7.6% of adults in Tompkins County to 16.1% in the Bronx. CDC PLACES, 2025 release (2023 estimates), SozoRock calculation.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:21.000
The map moves aside as bars grow: New Jersey 83.2%, Vermont 82.6%, Connecticut 60.0%, Massachusetts 58.7%, Pennsylvania 55.5%, United States 46.8%, and last, in orange, New York 35.4%. On-screen text: In shortage areas, New York meets 35% of primary-care need, the lowest among its neighbors. HRSA FY2026 Q4, Table 3.

4
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.500
Silence. Everything fades except one orange dot on a dim map. On-screen text: What if care came within reach?

5
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:35.000
An orange line travels from the dot to a marker labelled Purcell Integrative Osteopathic Care, Clifton Park, New York. On-screen text: A full year of direct primary care for up to 25 New Yorkers. Starting January 2027. Direct primary care. Ongoing telehealth. Transportation help. Health access education. With Dr. Michael Purcell. Clinical care stays with the licensed provider. Membership is not health insurance.

6
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:41.000
On a bright blue screen, 25 circles fill with orange one by one as a budget counter rises to $108,000. On-screen text: $4,320 supports one New Yorker for a full year. Funds are confirmed before anyone enrolls. Reports at months 3, 6, 9 and 12.

7
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:47.000
The field of dots returns with 25 orange dots among them. On-screen text: Up to 25 New Yorkers. One year. A start. End card: SozoRock Health. Care for every ZIP Code. Join the interest list. Sponsor a participant. health.sozorockfoundation.org.
